Deploying and Verifying the Application
==============
Configure for the lab environment
----------------
sed -i 's|http://127.0.0.1:5000|http://127.0.0.1:8080|g' job_board_app.py
sed -i 's|port=5000|port=8080|g' job_board_app.py
sed -i 's|host="127.0.0.1"|host="0.0.0.0"|g' job_board_app.py
sed -i 's|localhost:5000|localhost:8080|g' auth.py
sed -i 's|127.0.0.1:5000|127.0.0.1:8080|g' auth.py
sed -i 's/uvicorn.run(app, port=8001)/uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0", port=8000)/' auth_server.py
sed -i 's/host="localhost"/host="0.0.0.0"/g' mcp_server.py
sed -i 's/uvicorn.run(app,/uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0",/; s/port=8000/port=80/' mcp_server.py
sed -i 's|http://localhost:8000|http://localhost:80|g' job_board_app.py

Patch OAuth URLs so the browser uses the lab tunnel hostnames, not 127.0.0.1 (otherwise login redirects to your local machine):
==============
sed -i 's|AUTH_SERVER   = "http://127.0.0.1:8001"|AUTH_SERVER   = "https://devsecops-box-gpu-fmx9i8k5-8000.lab.practical-devsecops.training"|' job_board_app.py
sed -i 's|APP_URL       = "http://127.0.0.1:8080"|APP_URL       = "https://devsecops-box-gpu-fmx9i8k5-8080.lab.practical-devsecops.training"|' job_board_app.py
sed -i 's|http://127.0.0.1:8080/callback|https://devsecops-box-gpu-fmx9i8k5-8080.lab.practical-devsecops.training/callback|g' auth.py
sed -i 's|http://localhost:8080/callback|https://devsecops-box-gpu-fmx9i8k5-8080.lab.practical-devsecops.training/callback|g' auth.py

